1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,571
What happens if you drink too much water?

2
00:00:02,831 --> 00:00:05,240
Your kidneys can only process so much.

3
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:07,682
About one liter every hour, at best.

4
00:00:07,942 --> 00:00:10,807
Drink faster, and water backs up into your blood.

5
00:00:11,067 --> 00:00:12,600
Your blood gets diluted.

6
00:00:12,860 --> 00:00:15,777
Sodium, the salt balancing your fluids, drops.

7
00:00:16,037 --> 00:00:18,539
Water slides into your cells to rebalance.

8
00:00:18,799 --> 00:00:19,795
Your cells swell.

9
00:00:20,055 --> 00:00:21,406
Most cells can take it.

10
00:00:21,666 --> 00:00:22,955
Brain cells cannot.

11
00:00:23,215 --> 00:00:24,982
Your skull is a closed box.

12
00:00:25,242 --> 00:00:27,131
Swelling builds pressure inside it.

13
00:00:27,391 --> 00:00:29,752
That brings headache, confusion, seizures.

14
00:00:30,012 --> 00:00:31,466
It can even be fatal.

15
00:00:31,726 --> 00:00:34,537
Marathon runners and water contests proved it.

16
00:00:34,797 --> 00:00:36,011
So sip, don't flood.
